/-!
# Gorenstein morphisms of algebraic spaces and the étale local rings

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` and let `x` be a geometric
point of `X`. Then `f` is Gorenstein at the image of `x` exactly when the canonical
homomorphism of étale local rings

`𝒪_{Y, f ∘ x} ⟶ 𝒪_{X, x}`

is flat and the local ring of its fibre, the quotient of `𝒪_{X, x}` by the ideal generated by
the maximal ideal of `𝒪_{Y, f ∘ x}`, is Noetherian, local and Gorenstein.

## Main definitions

There are no new definitions. The ideal cutting out the local ring of the fibre is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.etaleLocalFiberIdeal`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isGorensteinAt_iff_etaleLocalRingMap`: **Stacks 0E15**, the
  equivalence of conditions (a) and (b) at a geometric point.

## Implementation notes

The criterion is one commuting square of pointed étale scheme charts of `f`, read on strict
henselizations. Affineness of the chart of the target is what makes the germs of its global
sections generate its local ring, which is what pins that square of henselizations down, so the
square is refined to one with affine target chart by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_compatible_affine_chart_square`; the identification of the étale
local rings with the strict henselizations of the chart local rings is Tag 04KF, and the
comparison of the two closed fibres across it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.nonempty_quotient_maximalIdeal_map_ringEquiv`. All three are the
generic halves of the Cohen–Macaulay case, Tag 0E0W, and are reused rather than repeated.

The Stacks text states the criterion under the standing hypothesis that the fibres of `f` are
locally Noetherian, but that hypothesis is not used: Noetherianity of the fibre local ring is
part of the germ predicate `AlgebraicGeometry.HasGorensteinFiberLocalRing` of Tag 0E13 rather
than an assumption, so the criterion is stated here without it. This matches
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsGorensteinAt` of Tag 0E14, which is likewise stated with no standing
hypothesis.

Two ring-theoretic inputs are Gorenstein-specific. That Gorensteinness of a Noetherian local
ring passes to and from a strict henselization is not available directly; it is derived here
from the content of Tag 0BJL, `Dualizing.isGorensteinLocalRing_iff_of_flat`, applied to the flat
local homomorphism into the strict henselization: its closed fibre is the residue field of the
strict henselization, hence regular, hence Gorenstein, so the three-term criterion collapses to
the two outer terms. That same criterion applied to a ring isomorphism, viewed as a flat local
homomorphism, transports Gorensteinness between universes, which the same-universe
`Stacks.Duality.isGorensteinLocalRing_ringEquiv_iff` cannot do; the étale local rings live one
universe above the chart stalks, so the transport is needed across universes. That the quotient
of a strict henselization by an extended ideal is a strict henselization of the quotient is
Tag 05WS.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E15](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E15)
